    "title_en": "Sensitivity of the SHiP experiment at CERN to sterile-neutrino-induced oscillations",
    "abstract_en": "The SHiP experiment, approved for the high-intensity beam-dump facility in the ECN3 hall at the CERN SPS in the North Area, will record neutrino interactions both in its scattering and neutrino detector (SND) and, about \\SI{70}m further downstream, in its calorimeter system. We show that the baseline SHiP detector configuration therefore forms a two-baseline experiment for oscillations induced by a sterile neutrino. From a \\textsc{Geant4} simulation of \\textsc{Genie}-generated interactions we derive the energy response of both stations to $\\nue$ and $\\numu$ charged-current (CC) interactions and the separation of $\\nue$~CC events from the neutral-current $\\pizero$ background, and fold them into a near/far disappearance analysis with a $20\\%$ flux-shape uncertainty and a $1\\%$ far/near normalisation uncertainty. For $6\\times10^{20}$ protons on target, the projected $95\\%$~CL median sensitivities are $\\Umufour\\simeq\\UmuLimit$ at $\\mfour\\simeq\\UmuLimitMass$~eV and $\\Uefour\\simeq\\UeLimit$ at $\\mfour\\simeq\\UeLimitMass$~eV. In the muon channel this lies below existing $\\numu$-disappearance limits for $\\DnineLow\\lesssim\\mfour\\lesssim\\DnineHigh$~eV.",
